body:
Lead: #4, #6, #7 and #8 are merged and ready for your verification. Main is at f3e624a, nothing pushed. The suite passes: CPython 156 tests (34 hou-only skipped), hython 156 OK.
- Reviews: all four approved, minor findings only. I fixed #7's two nits myself (ebd0648): .p3d stripping belongs to the Proxy node, and a note that Buoyancy/PhysX mass rules come from D14 rather than A3OB.
- #8 minors not fixed yet:
  - import doesn't warn on 0-2-sided faces â†’ folded into #12;
  - no re-read on file mtime (only path change or the Reload button);
  - selections containing proxy points create empty or partial mesh groups, with the members kept inside the proxy's embedded groups. M4 must rebuild those selections from both places.
- Small change on main (f3e624a): nodes.KINDS now discovers node modules by itself, so parallel node tasks don't conflict.
- Running now, wf_5afa5623-68c, implement then review:
  - #9 Extract LOD + Assemble LODs (pass-through and edit tests);
  - #10 LOD Properties + Material Assign;
  - #11 Mass + Proxy (Proxy must match the importer's proxy form);
  - #12 Selection browser shelf tool + import polish.
That completes M3 per ux-tools Â§9. I'll ping you after the merge.
